// ios/SPEC.md Section 4.3 — the server origin is a build setting, not a game
// constant. It answers "which deployment does this build talk to", not a
// rate limit, radius, threshold, tolerance or timeout, so CLAUDE.md's
// constants rule keeps it out of packages/shared entirely; it lives here
// instead. It is the same value the server holds as PUBLIC_ORIGIN
// (SPEC.md 4.3).
//
// The $() is xcconfig's way of writing // without opening a comment: a bare
// // here would end the line, and the value would silently become
// "https:".
SERVER_ORIGIN = https:/$()/tipsytrails.ahultsch.com

// WKAppBoundDomains (Info.plist) is a static array and cannot compute a
// host from a URL at build time, so the host is repeated here as its own
// setting rather than derived from SERVER_ORIGIN above. SERVER_HOST and
// SERVER_ORIGIN are one value in two shapes and must be edited together —
// nothing in this file enforces that, only the comment does; the actual
// check is packages/tracker/src/ios-config.test.ts, which reads both and
// fails if SERVER_ORIGIN stops ending in SERVER_HOST.
SERVER_HOST = tipsytrails.ahultsch.com

// The owner's Apple Developer team ID. Left empty here — never a secret or
// signing material in the repository (C6) — and filled in by
// Server.local.xcconfig, which is gitignored and read by project.yml's
// automatic-signing settings.
DEVELOPMENT_TEAM =
